ysis of artemethe-lumefantrine for treatment of uncomplicated malaria in Zambia</article-title><source>Malar J</source><year>2007</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>21</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17313682</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1475-2875-6-21</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chanda</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Sikaala</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kapelwa</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Moonga</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Njunju</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Macdonald</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Thea</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamer</surname><given-names>DH</given-names></name><name><surname>Sipilanyambe</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assesment of the therapeutic efficacy of artemether-lumefantrine (Coartem<sup>&#x000ae;</sup>) and sulphadoxine-pyrimethamine (SP)-artesunate in Zambian children</article-title><source>Proceedings of the 53rd Annual Meeting of the Society of Tropical Medicine and Hygiene, 7 &#x02013; 11 November 2004, Miami, FL</source><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Utzinger</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tozan</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Doumani</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>BH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The economic pay off of integrated malaria control in the Zambian Copperbelt between 1930 and 1950</article-title><source>Trop Med Int Health</source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>657</fpage><lpage>677</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1